T:Crawl through, green branch: Hungarian arch game
C:traditional (Hungary)
O:Hungary, Baranya county
R:children's game
S:Kiss Áron, Magyar gyermekjáték-gyűjtemény (Budapest, 1891), Újhold-játék No. 4, p. 207
N:THE GAME (Kiss p. 206, No. 1, the same game): "Két gyermek összefogódzik, kezöket magasra fölemelik, azaz kaput alkotnak kezeikből. A többiek szintén összefogódzanak egy sorba, és átbújnak a kapun": two children join hands and raise them high, making a gate; the others join hands in a line and pass through it. At the end the gatekeepers must not let the last one through, but catch her and stand her beside the gatekeeper on the left; and so on until all are caught.
N:THE PLATE: No. 4, one flat, 2/4, three staves; the first four bars with a repeat and two lines of words (the passers, then the gatekeepers); the last eight bars ending "raj-ta, raj-ta, raj-ta, raj-ta .. (a hány átbúvó van)" (as many as pass through). "(Baranya.)"
N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): printed p. 207 rendered at 300 dpi from the MEK PDF; staff lines found by row darkness; every head found along each staff and measured against the lines, the uncertain ones read again beside the lines found at that note; every bar checked to make two quarters.
N:UNCERTAIN: none in the notes; tempo ours.
